Gemmont on-board GCC examples
=============================

Compile and run Hello World:

  gcc -O0 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/hello.c -o /tmp/hello
  /tmp/hello

Compile and draw VGA color bars:

  gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/vga-colorbars.c -o /tmp/vga-colorbars
  /tmp/vga-colorbars

Compile and draw NT35510 LCD color bars:

  gcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror \
    /usr/share/gemmont-examples/lcd-colorbars.c -o /tmp/lcd-colorbars
  /tmp/lcd-colorbars

The examples find the framebuffer names "Xilinx" and "chiplab-lcd", so they do
not depend on whether Linux registers VGA or LCD as /dev/fb0. Pass an explicit
/dev/fbN path to override discovery. Use the serial console to enter commands;
both displays remain output devices until a keyboard controller is added.
